{"kind":"assert","text":"Builder's readiness judgment for starting artroom-jam, dated 2026-10-04 (request b4ef9b7a). Not yet. The platform can do what the first task needs on the integration branch; it cannot yet be used from the jam's repository. Two things are missing, and neither is a new capability to build.\n\nThe first task, as the jam note names it (section 9, \"Starting development\"): found a jam development room, move it to a v2 document with workroom declarations, and land the jam's own declarations and acceptance cases through generic acts and independent reviews.\n\nWhat that task uses, and the evidence at a10c9bec on request/test-overhead (gate: 2,033 tests pass):\n- A room becomes v2 by landing a v2 document. Room test \"a room moves from v1 to v2 by landing a v2 document ...\". Stage 2, approved 9cb05da9 at 39430e23.\n- Acts of kinds the client was not built for, signed with their binding, over HTTPS and MCP, and from the command line. Room tests \"the client signs v: 2 with the binding the caller read ...\" and \"a bearer reads the declarations with acts, and performs a kind that has no named tool with act ...\"; CLI tests in packages/cli/test/declared.test.ts. Stage 5, in review at 736f4953.\n- Review and land by separate members, with grants that never gain a kind. Stage 2's grant and session tests.\n- A published log of a v2 room that verifies. Room test \"the declared path writes no row more ... the log of the v2 session publishes and verifies\". Stage 3, delivered in part.\n- A change of vocabulary at an exact activation, with old records read under their own declarations. Room tests \"old records are read under the declarations of their own seq\".\n\nWhat the first task does not use: stage 4's primitives (reservation, hand-over, fixed scope, hold modes), the checker service signing v2 jobs, complete carry accounting, the musical fixture, and the two spikes J1 and J2.\n\nWhat is missing.\n1. The code is not on main and not deployed. The jam depends on Artroom only through a deployed room's URL and published packages. The deployed spike runs main, which has stage 1 only, and unreviewed admission code is not deployed. Needed: the integration branch landed and the spike redeployed. Owners: the lane reviews in flight (stage 5 229e1e80, bearer 510fbbbf, MCP core awaiting the planner's contract artifacts), and the planner's decision 18060abc on landing while stage 3's condition 2 is open.\n2. The packages cannot be installed from outside this repository. npm view @generalbusiness/artroom-client answers 404, and every package is version 0.0.0. Needed: the client, CLI, MCP, contract and policy packages installable by the jam repository, from a registry or as packed tarballs. Owner: request f3299ab4 (the public-package starter and its availability inventory), not yet promised.\n\nRemaining limits that the first task can live with, each with its owner: complete carry accounting (1e8fee4b with 48c021ea, amendment review 85032553); the UI's Acts page is not wired to a live room (stage 5 limits); recover has no client surface; a room is founded v1 and moved to v2 by a landing, until a13a0bf5.\n\nI will record the judgment again when 1 and 2 are done, and then start the first task with tracked work in the jam's room. The manual (db2fd146) starts with it."}